  "source_cause": [
    "Original toWcnf emits nVars() in header but omits satisfied clauses and false literals; declared trailing variables can be unused in exported clauses.",
    "Original DIMACS header records vars but does not reserve them; readClause allocates only through highest referenced literal. Original addClause_ allocates no new variables.",
    "Original parser compares declared vars to S.nVars() at end of parse, prior to later soft normalization/search; actual Main pre-search statistics in all30 equal literalMax and remain below declaration.",
    "This is original unchanged downstream parser/export behavior for valid unused declared variables, not new soft-unit auxiliary creation during readClause. Same exact warning exists in both roles; clause count/range/weights valid and all Main optimal/status agree with independent Pauli truth."
  ],
  "proposal": "Allow ONLY exact audited60-byte warning for the30 identified live-WCNF Main observations when header/count/ranges valid, literalMax<declared, Main reported nVars==literalMax and all original scientific fields remain checked; retain strict empty stderr for targeted/reused Main and reject every other diagnostic. No production/parser/WCNF/raw rewrite.",
